A||||12||GT Bastard||In case you're interested... Progress on my SE(1FST2M6's old car.)||||1||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||06-01-2001||11:11 AM||||So anyhow, it's been waiting for a new motor ever since I got it from 1FST(Travis) and I finally got something together.  The new 3.1 shortblock is nearly complete at the machine shop, and I've torn the top-end off the car so that I can have the heads blasted, ported, polished, etc...  It's getting a new ACT kush-loc clutch with Napa pressure plate and t/o bearing.  The motor is just a 2.8 bored .030 over with hypereutectic pistons and chrome moly rings.  Using 1.5 Crower full roller rocker arms.  It'll be interesting to see what it'll do.  1FST pulled a best of 14.7 in the 1/4 without NOS.  I took it to the track a couple weeks ago with the car running like crap.  I did it because I wanted a baseline before tearing it apart.  The car smoked the whole way down the track, and the bearings rattled like hell.  Best I could muster was 15.9@87mph.  I have now discovered the the rear brakes drag, and two spark plug electrodes were MELTED!!!  Funny thing is, the car ran pretty smooth, and I'm positive that it wasn't missing.  The air fuel meter wasn't showing a lean condition, but it appears as though two injectors aren't doing their job.  The two cylinders with the melted plugs have very clean pistons(lean condition/no carbon build-up.)  My 60ft times were all right at 2 seconds though, so the car really didn't seem to lack power off the line(4.10 gears and full race clutch.)  It really didn't fall on it's ass till 3rd gear.  Anyhow, I'm still driving my GT but I hope to have the SE done soon.  I'll have pics and stuff soon.  Later all!  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtbastard.gif">     <P>"My heroes are John Wayne, the Simpsons, and whoever canceled Full House/Bob Saget."||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||06-01-2001||06:33 PM||||What happened to the 3.1 stroker you planned? There is no such thing a Chrome-molly rings only molly rings. It probably didn't misfire because of the MSD multi-spark ignition you have. <P>You can send the injectors out to <A HREF="http://www.injector.com" TARGET=_blank>www.injector.com</A>  and they can rebuild or blueprint your injectors for you. <P>Good luck with your engine. <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||06-01-2001||06:51 PM||||You might be right on the MSD....  And yes, it IS a 3.1 stroker.  Hmmmm... My Summit reciept calls them chrome-moly rings.... Oh well, no matter.  The 2.8 shortblock is still in the car, just the top-end was pulled so far.  My 3.1 stroker is already being assembled using a different 2.8 block.  The 2.8 block is being bored .030 over, and I'm using Firebird 3.1 pistons and a Lumina APV crank(3.1)||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||06-01-2001||09:08 PM||||Don't forget ARP rod bolts and Main studs for your bottom-end strength especially if you’re running nitrous again. The part number for the Main studs is 233-5602. I don't remember the rod bolt numbers but they are easy to find. The fierosore I think sells them.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||06-02-2001||06:30 PM||||Already went with ARP bolts... And no, there won't be any NOS on this motor.  After careful consideration, I've decided against it.||||reg||1
